# =============================================================================
# EXPERIMENT DECLARATION — phase1_open3d_reference   (scaffolded by `api.py declare`)
#
# This file is YOURS until `reconstruct.py` seals it: edit the label, trim
# add setting overrides. After assessment the student section is
# digest-sealed — a new idea is a NEW file under a NEW name (§3.1).
#
# PREDICTION (write BEFORE assessing — the seal makes it non-retractable):
#   pipeline: Full original 191-frame capture. Weak geometry and depth loss
#             may reduce correspondence support, especially near frames 100-114.
#   baseline: Hypothesis: recognizable map, Mean L2 below 0.20 m; failure is
#             possible and will be retained without tuning. Compare backend
#             accuracy and runtime under the same measurement harness.
#   treatment: icpBackend=open3d; voxel_size_m=0.05; seed=0; no filtering.
#   controls: Same RGB-D, RANSAC, normal/FPFH radii and matching thresholds.
#             Native backend stopping rules remain unchanged (custom 60 max,
#             Open3D 100 max), so this compares existing implementations.
# =============================================================================

